================================================================================
WHICH LICENSE APPLIES TO WHAT
================================================================================

  kmod/                    GPL-2.0-only
                           Not a choice. These are Linux kernel modules, they
                           call GPL-only exported symbols such as
                           register_kprobe, and every one of them declares
                           MODULE_LICENSE("GPL"). They cannot be shipped under
                           a weaker licence.

  scripts/  lib/           MIT  (full text below)
  vgpu.conf.example

  docs/  notes/            CC-BY-4.0
  README.md                https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  REFERENCES.md            Attribution required for any public use, not only
                           for redistributing the files.

  host-config/             MIT, as above.

Not covered by any of this, because it is not mine to license: the NVIDIA vGPU
host driver, the GRID guest driver, their installers, vgpuConfig.xml, and any
NVIDIA licence file. None of those are in this repository. See REFERENCES.md
for the third-party projects this builds on, which carry their own licences.

